  "notes": "Block-13 fields in FORM-366 FIELDS input appear garbled/misaligned (cause 'S', system 'stem', component 'Com', manufacturer 'onent') and are copied verbatim per instructions but are not meaningful; cause_code remains TBD/provisional per the official form. Narrative identifies BPV #1 failing open due to fast-open SOV coil (TGF-SOV-BV-1) internal short from a wiring weak point; the other two coils were inspected and found sound, so no separate failure mode was created for them. Operator misdiagnosis (initially treating symptom as EH leak) is modeled as a distinct parallel failure mode contributing to the consequence, per narrative's 'gap in symptom-based response' cause discussion, though official cause code stays TBD/S per form. No previous similar-event LER cited (station states none in past 10 years) so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge created. ECCS, main condenser, and feedwater systems were mentioned only as available mitigating systems supporting safe shutdown in a general safety-significance statement without being part of the failure chain; per rule 6 they are treated as available backups to the shutdown/consequence rather than to a specific inoperable safety system - omitted since no direct BACKED_UP_BY target system tied to the failure exists (the failure led to scram, not to an ECCS demand)."
